---
name: hax-rust
description: |
  Generate Rust code that compiles and passes the Hax type checker for formal verification extraction.
  Use when:
  (1) Writing Rust code for Hax extraction to Lean 4/F*/Coq/ProVerif
  (2) Creating formally verifiable cryptographic implementations
  (3) Converting regular Rust to Hax-compatible Rust
  (4) Building high-assurance security software

  This skill works as a layer ON TOP of rust-analyzer (not replacing it).
  Hax accepts a subset of Safe Rust with specific restrictions.
version: 2.0.0
dependencies:
  - rust-analyzer-lsp  # For code intelligence
  - lean-lsp-mcp       # Optional: for Lean proof development
tools:
  - hax_syntax_check   # Fast tree-sitter validation
  - hax_cargo_check    # Full cargo hax validation
  - hax_extract        # Extract to proof backends
triggers:
  - "hax"
  - "formal verification"
  - "extractable rust"
  - "proof assistant"
  - "verified cryptography"
---

<!-- Include main documentation -->
